# Backend Rules

- Use ASP.NET Core minimal APIs or controllers consistently; do not mix casually.
- Use dependency injection for services.
- Keep endpoints thin — map routes in `Endpoints/` and delegate to Application services.
- Put business logic in the Application layer, not in endpoints or Infrastructure.
- Keep LLM provider code behind `IAssistantClient` and related interfaces.
- Do not let frontend-specific concepts leak into backend models or Contracts.
- Use strongly typed request/response DTOs in `JeffyGPT.Contracts`.
- Use async APIs for I/O.
- Use structured logging.
- Do not log secrets, prompts containing private data, API keys, or full model responses unless explicitly configured.

## Conditionals

- Prefer named predicate/helper functions over inline compound boolean expressions when the condition encodes domain, security, or protocol rules.
- Use `private static` helpers on the owning type for single-class logic.
- Use `internal static` helpers plus `InternalsVisibleTo` for pure predicates that deserve direct unit tests.
- Prefer shared helpers or options methods when the same condition appears in two or more places.

## Project layout

| Project | Responsibility |
|---------|----------------|
| `JeffyGPT.Api` | HTTP host, CORS, endpoint mapping, DI registration |
| `JeffyGPT.Application` | Orchestration, validation, interfaces |
| `JeffyGPT.Contracts` | Shared DTOs |
| `JeffyGPT.Infrastructure` | External integrations, LLM clients (`Chat/`), MCP client (`Mcp/`), tool executor (`Tools/`) |
| `JeffyMCP` | Standalone MCP server hosting tools |

Register services via `AddApplication()` and `AddInfrastructure()` extension methods. MCP client + tool executor register via `AddMcpTools()` in `Infrastructure/Mcp/McpDependencyInjection.cs`. Tool implementations live in `src/JeffyMCP/` (see `.roots/docs/jeffymcp.md`).
